# Typography: Line breaking simple (greedy) and optimal (the whole paragraph at once) on a narrow justified column.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Typography · Line breaking
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Styles:
		For style: row
			Gap: 30
			Vertical: top
		For style: column
			Box:
				Width: 191.5
				Padding: 0 0 0 6
				Border: 0 0 0 0.5
				Border color: rule
			Typography:
				Font: IBM Plex Serif
				Align: justify
	Section:
		Text: Typography
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Line breaking
		Paragraph: With `Line breaking: simple`, the default, each line takes as many words as fit. With `optimal`, the engine chooses the breaks of the whole paragraph at once and leaves more even spaces, which shows above all in narrow justified text.
			Style: intro
		Stack:
			Style: row
			Item:
				Block:
					Text: Line breaking: simple
						Style: label
					Paragraph: The association is also organizing a walk along the river, starting from the old bridge at ten in the morning. Registration is open until Friday at the public library, and the route is suitable for children and for the elderly.
						Style: column
						Typography:
							Line breaking: simple
			Item:
				Block:
					Text: Line breaking: optimal
						Style: label
					Paragraph: The association is also organizing a walk along the river, starting from the old bridge at ten in the morning. Registration is open until Friday at the public library, and the route is suitable for children and for the elderly.
						Style: column
						Typography:
							Line breaking: optimal
